  "decidedBy": "the project owner, 2026-09-26, asking for the kings of Judah and Israel side by side with the prophets who spoke in their days, and for Zerubbabel and Shealtiel to list the prophets of their time too",
  "policy": "A prophet is set in a ruler's days only where a verse puts him there: the heading of his book, a word dated by the ruler's year, the history bringing the two together, or the chronicle naming him as the one who wrote the reign's acts. A span of years that merely overlaps is not a statement and is not recorded. The same holds for the rulers of the nations the text brings into a reign, and for the year of the other kingdom's king in which each king began to reign. Where the verse speaks of the ruler as 'the king', 'he' or 'him', the ruler is the one the passage has just named.",
  "method": "manual",
